  "foaf:name": "Borneo Ocean Resilience 4Nature, Economy, Outreach",
  "sdo:name": "Borneo Ocean Resilience 4Nature, Economy, Outreach",
  "sdo:description": "Our Ocean Decade Action restores and protects Brunei and Borneo’s coasts through science, innovation, and community engagement. From 2025–2030, we will deploy 2,000+ artificial reefs to deter illegal trawling, rebuild fisheries, and buffer erosion. Community-led mangrove planting with AI/IoT monitoring will boost blue carbon and resilience, while Brunei’s first oyster hatchery and pilot sea kelp projects improve water quality, create livelihoods, and generate carbon credits. Coastal protection will be enhanced through living breakwaters and reef-based defenses guided by hydrodynamic and particle-tracking models. AI, eDNA, and satellite/seabed data will drive monitoring, fisheries recovery, and IUU detection. Education with students, citizen science diving, and youth programs anchor stewardship. Together, these actions form a Brunei-Borneo Ocean Action Framework for climate resilience, biodiversity restoration, and a sustainable blue economy across the South China Sea.",
